This comparison covers c. 1847–1950. Logical relationships can be represented by symbols, switches and explicit instructions. Compare an abstract procedure with a machine that carries it out.

C0159 | atlas-focused-sessions-v6/objective/computing-session-2/objectives
Can a program always tell whether another will stop?
How can a machine correct its actions?

C0160 | atlas-focused-sessions-v6/entry fallback/computing-session-2/motivation; atlas-focused-sessions-v6/story body/computing-session-2/entryCue.text
